y  similarities to his with her mom leaving  and her dad dying after he married  angela that she gets it they both feel  like they don't fit anywhere and they're  on the outside looking in and they agree  that that can mess you up they have a  connection and they hook up and when  they lay back on the bed you can see  that harrison has the straight razor in  his back pocket the next morning angela  finds him in audrey's bed and drives him  home it's another thing to point out how  dex lacks even the basic parental  instincts not knowing what to do about  it he shifts his focus on molly instead  things take an interesting turn there  when he runs into her talking to kurt at  the tavern he plugs in his phone using  the charger at the bar and records their  conversation he then follows them when  he sees them leaving and listens to what  they were saying kurt admits that he  lied about the facetime and claims that  matt is hiding out at his cabin he  offers to let molly interview him if she  doesn't tell anyone where she's going so  he's luring her to the middle of nowhere  with no one knowing where she's at and  as he approaches dexter notices a very  serious serial killer vibe about the  whole situation he sees them going  through the basement and he has a moment  there where he thinks that he could just  let her die and then she would be out of  his hair for good but decides that he  should intervene instead  while they're in the hallway on the way  to the room molly is starting to get  freaked out and just in time dex opens  the storm door kurt is surprised but has  to pretend and gets even more upset when  dexter forces his way in to get a look  at the room he's able to get molly out  of there she now thinks he's a good guy  and he now knows that kurt is the serial  killer that angela has been looking for  she's at the caves with teddy searching  while everyone else is at the wrestling  match things get crazy there when  harrison gets head-butted and even  though 